Human: Can you tell me the steps to write an if/then statement in C programming language?

Assistant: Sure! An “if/then” statement is used to test a condition, and execute a block of code if the condition is true and a block of code if the condition is false. In C, you do this by writing:
if (condition) {
    // code to execute if condition equals true
}
or if you want to call a particular block of code even if the condition is not true, you just write:

if (condition) {
    block of code to execute
}
but if statement are often best in this form.
